    "specific_statement": "Must name at least one behavior-specific action, expected outcome, or changed relationship attributable to the behavior. Merely naming a file/component, promising general coverage, or listing an unexplained flag is insufficient. A statement about part of a multi-condition contract is counted with an explicit scope_note, never called full understanding.",
    "plan": "A specific statement that also commits to a concrete test or assertion change. Behavior recognition alone, a search intention, a hypothetical test possibility, or a post-edit claim is not a pre-edit test plan.",
    "negative_coding": "No qualifying statement means none observed in recorded public messages, not failure to understand. An empty client trace is unavailable, not silence. All per-run public messages are read before recording an empty statements list.",
    "delivery": "Join the existing patch_semantics without changing labels. Missing concerns the submitted patch; unchanged-suite protection and dynamic consequences remain unknown.",
    "receipt_evidence": "Existing exact source-anchor matches are a separate code-line availability measure, not a semantic-completeness or comprehension label.",
    "aggregation": "Report behavior-agent counts, episodes, repositories and production families. Inspect successful and omitted outputs under identical statement criteria. Do not interpret these observational associations as causes."
